feat: Multi-step approval workflows for work orders

Adds a multi-step approval engine that gates work-order transitions
behind configurable policies. Approvers see a queue with full WO
context, approve/reject with a comment, and the engine walks ordered
steps until final approval re-applies the original transition or
rejection rolls the WO back to its previous status.

Schema (prisma)
  - ApprovalPolicy / ApprovalPolicyStep / ApprovalRequest /
    ApprovalDecision models
  - ApprovalTrigger (PRE_START / PRE_CLOSE / VENDOR_QUOTE),
    ApprovalStatus, ApprovalOutcome enums
  - PENDING_APPROVAL added to WorkOrderStatus
  - 4 new permissions seeded: work_orders.approve_budget,
    .approve_safety, .approve_vendor, .manage_approvals
    (Owner gets all 4, Admin gets all 4, Technician none)

Engine (lib/approvals)
  - engine.ts: findApplicablePolicy, openApprovalRequest,
    submitDecision, cancelApprovalRequest with full step-walking,
    requireAll semantics, and rollback on rejection
  - notify.ts: emails to all eligible approvers when a step opens,
    final-state email to the requester

API
  - GET/POST /api/approval-policies
  - GET/PATCH/DELETE /api/approval-policies/[id]
  - GET /api/approval-requests (with ?mine=1, ?status, ?workOrderId)
  - GET/DELETE /api/approval-requests/[id]
  - POST /api/approval-requests/[id]/decide

Work Order PATCH hook
  - Transitions to IN_PROGRESS / COMPLETED that match an active
    policy park the WO in PENDING_APPROVAL and open a request.
  - work_orders.manage_approvals + ?bypass=1 break-glass override.
  - Returns 409 if a request is already open for the WO.

UI
  - /approvals (user-side, sidebar nav after Reports) — My Queue +
    All Requests tabs, full decision history per request,
    Approve/Reject modal with optional comment
  - /settings/approvals (Settings → Approvals) — list + create + edit
    + delete + pause/resume policies, up to 10 ordered steps each,
    priority/type/minTotalCost match criteria
  - PENDING_APPROVAL added to admin work-orders status palette
  - Mobile responsive: max-w-2xl modal, modal-safe-pad,
    flex-wrap action buttons

Handbook
  - Work Orders chapter — Approval workflows section rewritten with
    full feature description plus a worked setup example
  - Roadmap — bullet removed (feature shipped)

19 files: 7 modified, 12 added.
